{
  "_comment": [
    "EXPERIMENT SET — 18 publishers not covered by our RSS/API feeds, spanning regions and",
    "viewpoints. This file is NOT the shipped config (crawler_publishers.json) and nothing loads it",
    "unless you pass --config. It exists so the experiment can run without changing what a deploy",
    "would ship.",
    "",
    "PURPOSE: the first six publishers were almost entirely Anglo-American, and three of the four",
    "with real volume (AP, BBC, HuffPost) block ClaudeBot and anthropic-ai by name. That may be an",
    "industry norm or it may be an Anglo-American one. This set is the test — Europe, Asia, the",
    "Middle East, Africa, Latin America and Oceania, with leans from -1 to +1.",
    "",
    "ROUND 1 IS DELIBERATELY SECTION-ONLY. Guessing 18 sitemap URLs would repeat the HuffPost",
    "mistake at scale (2 of 3 guesses wrong). robots.txt DECLARES a publisher's sitemaps, and the",
    "verifier reports them whatever we configure — so run the verifier first, read the declared",
    "sitemap URLs out of its output, and fill them in for round 2. A section URL is the one thing",
    "safe to guess: it is the homepage or a top-level news index.",
    "",
    "THE ARTICLE PATTERNS ARE GUESSES from public URL convention and have never been tested against",
    "these sites. The verifier grades them: 0% is a blocker, >98% means it is not filtering, and the",
    "healthy band so far has been 23-83%. Expect several to be wrong.",
    "",
    "Every publisher resolves to an outlet-registry canonical name, so discovered URLs would carry",
    "the right identity and lean. Nothing here is wired into a poller; plan mode only."
  ],
  "publishers": [
    {
      "publisher": "Le Monde",
      "domains": ["lemonde.fr"],
      "sources": [{"kind": "section", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/"}],
